How is the child survival rate and USAID funding related? Learn more here: Lancet

About: 
Learn geography the maybe hopeful, maybe depressing way.

Last time I had a baby, it was kind of hard mentally not to be constantly thinking about parents losing children. This time I listened to a lot of Dear John and Hank podcasts and gave myself a project and it's gone a lot better.

I ended up making a geography website with an obvious angle. The goal is educating on how child mortality is a solvable problem, but hopefully in a respectful and engaging way. But it's really hard to get the tone right. If anyone has feedback on how this could be more effective, I'd love to hear it. 

Also, obviously, I just wanted to share this for my one chance to have someone beside the bots see this.

I do know from experience that the build-it-and-they-will-come does not work with random website, so to make a actual positive change, I'm making lots of small monthly donations. This was very much more to keep my mind occupied. 

Also, I made a USAID budget website years ago that only ever got Russian porn bots as comments, so I honestly would like a few people besides my lovely husband and daughter to see it. 


I made a geography website that also doubles as way to learn about child survival rates and USAID. 

Many Americans don't realize that humanitarian aid, when focused on diseases and nutrition, is extremely effective. And they also don't realize that the funding for humanitarian aid is only about 1% of the budget. I hope this website is a way for people to learn this, but ever-so-slightly slant-wise. I also wanted this to feel engaging, while being respectful to the life-altering suffering behind even the low percentage of child-mortality. If you have ideas on how I could achieve this better, or just any general comments, I'd love to hear it. 

I would also like to set up similiar learning website, ad-free, with a bird or tree identification game, which won't lead itself as naturally as geography to educating on child mortality. In that case, I was think of just a note that life is full of wonderous things to love, like birds, and if you want more children to get a live a beautiful life, please call your representive about USAID funding. 
